{"metric":"majumdar_papapetrou","source":[{"metric":"majumdar_papapetrou","system":"isotropic","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"dd43ce9604475380"},{"metric":"rn_metric","system":"spherical","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"4a17df0330938cb8"}],"views":[{"id":"one_hole","label":"One hole","box":[-3.5916,3.5916,-3.2416,9.5248],"system":"isotropic","fade":{"top":0.9,"bottom":0.9},"settings":"$m = 1$, the unit of every length; inside the horizon, Reissner-Nordström's own chart at $r_s = 2m$ and $r_q = m$, where its $r$ is the areal radius $R$.","caption":["One hole alone ($U = 1 + m/r$), which is the extremal Reissner-Nordström black hole, maximally extended, each point in the diagram a 2-sphere of areal radius $R = r + m$. The extension is a tower of exteriors and interiors that repeats up and down without end. Outside the horizon the tortoise coordinate is $r_* = r + 2m\\ln(r/m) - m^2/r$, and inside it $R_* = R + 2m\\ln|R/m - 1| - m^2/(R - m) - m$, which vanishes at $R = 0$.","We place each region by $p = \\arctan(u/m)$ and $q = \\arctan(v/m)$ with $u, v = ct \\mp r_*$, shifted by $\\pi$ from one region to the next. The horizon is a double root of $g^{rr}$, where the surface gravity vanishes, and the map is continuous across it. The singularity $R = 0$ is timelike and lies on the vertical line $X = -\\pi$.","The coordinates $t$ and $r > 0$ cover one exterior. Its moment $t = 0$ runs from spatial infinity down the infinitely long throat toward the corner $X = -\\pi$, $T = 0$, where the past and future horizons meet at an infinite distance."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[-0.1,-3.2416],[0.0,-3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[-3.1416,-3.2416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[3.1416,0.0]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416